back merges ran three full CI passes, two of them on\nalready-outdated commits.\n- Group push runs by `github.ref` with `cancel-in-progress`, so a new\nmerge cancels the superseded in-progress run.\n- PR runs keep the per-PR cancelling group. Schedule and\n`workflow_dispatch` runs keep the per-sha queueing group: concurrent\noxc-PR dispatches must queue rather than cancel each other, and a\nscheduled run cancelled by a push only skips the green-marker record,\nwhich the record job already treats as \"one extra run later\".","tree":{"sha":"04cbec3765e3aacd25e40609643d465b4b06b7ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/git/trees/04cbec3765e3aacd25e40609643d465b4b06b7ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/git/commits/c8b37f5114f518932f741be6b90fc22860257d62","verification":{"payload":"tree 04cbec3765e3aacd25e40609643d465b4b06b7ae\nparent 299cdd03c6610ef0ebc9db549adedf539a1debf2\nauthor Dunqing <dengqing0821@gmail.com> 1783614094 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783614094 +0800\n\nci: cancel superseded main runs on push (#193)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Pushes to main currently group CI by `github.sha`, so each merge gets\nits own concurrency group and nothing is ever cancelled — three\nback-to-back merges ran three full CI passes, two of them on\nalready-outdated commits.\n- Group push runs by `github.ref` with `cancel-in-progress`, so a new\nmerge cancels the superseded in-progress run.\n- PR runs keep the per-PR cancelling group. Schedule and\n`workflow_dispatch` runs keep the per-sha queueing group: concurrent\noxc-PR dispatches must queue rather than cancel each other, and a\nscheduled run cancelled by a push only skips the green-marker record,\nwhich the record job already treats as \"one extra run later\".","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT8qOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzBMQAEPEiJTc1OIVIk9f5a49jxp8\nm1v6qNjazAmsgB3kPtj1QY+vQ5HpoO8iI5hfVlYh0x96hws0pW3LtgBhjotoJu+v\n+eBRhUdDq6nU