"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commits/299cdd03c6610ef0ebc9db549adedf539a1debf2"}],"sha":"c8b37f5114f518932f741be6b90fc22860257d62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commits/c8b37f5114f518932f741be6b90fc22860257d62"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29533304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Dunqing","id":29533304,"login":"Dunqing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NTMzMzA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commits/299cdd03c6610ef0ebc9db549adedf539a1debf2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T16:07:05Z","email":"dengqing0821@gmail.com","name":"Dunqing"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T16:07:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: run pinned repo test suites against minified sources (#191)\n\nSecond half of the runtime-correctness work (stacked on the bundle diff oracle PR, which carries the shared `runtime-minify` subcommand): run real repos'' own test suites against their minified sources.\n\n## Repo suites (`Test Runtime (<name>)`, 5 matrix rows)\n\nThe set favors framework monorepos with huge suites — vue (3,607 tests), svelte (7,557), solid (482) — plus es-toolkit and zod (big TS libraries). Repos whose tests import built dist (vitest, astro) are structurally out of scope: the classifier''s `git checkout` restore can''t rebuild gitignored dist, so this oracle is src-alias repos only. Per row:\n\n1. **Checkout** the pinned repo (pins in [`runtime-repos.json`](./runtime-repos.json)) into `target-repo/`; the pin means the only variable is oxc itself.\n2. **Install** via `scripts/runtime-test.mjs install <name> target-repo` (per-entry quirks documented in `notes`).\n3. **Minify in place** with `runtime-minify` — filenames/extensions preserved, so minified JS inside a `.ts` file flows through vitest/jest transpilation untouched. Only shipped source is matched, never tests: original assertions run against minified implementation.\n4. **Classify** differentially:\n\n```\nrun suite on minified sources\n├─ green ──────────────────────────→ pass\n└─ red → rerun once\n   ├─ green ───────────────────────→ pass (flake absorbed)\n   └─ red → git checkout -- .  → run suite unminified\n      ├─ green → FAIL   ← real minifier/transformer bug\n      └─ red   → pass + ::warning::  (env/flake rot, not oxc)\n```\n\nA row can only fail when the identical tests on the identical machine pass unminified and fail minified — upstream breakage and flaky tests are structurally unable to produce a false red. TS repos route through `oxc_transformer` first, so the oracle also catches transformer runtime bugs. A weekly workflow (`bump-runtime-repos.yml`) re-pins repos whose HEAD baseline passes, via PR, so CI on the bump PR validates new pins minified before merge.\n\n## Notes\n\n- **It already caught a real upstream bug — in vite, not oxc**: vetting the vue entry produced 377 deterministic failures that initially looked like a mangler scope collision. Systematic follow-up exonerated oxc (697/697 references bind identically; plain Node runs the minified file) and pinned the real cause: vite''s `ssrTransform` doesn''t treat `switch` blocks as lexical scopes, so switch-case `let`s mis-scope and same-named import references are left un-rewritten. Fixed upstream in vitejs/vite#22893; the one file is `ignore`d with the full analysis in its `notes` (remove when the fix propagates to rolldown-vite). Cross-check: terser''s output triggers the same vite bug; esbuild/swc escape only by name-allocation luck.\n- Process rule encoded by that episode: a red verdict gets plain-node confirmation before blaming oxc — the suite''s own module-transform layer is part of the executed stack.\n- Runtime rows skip the monitor-oxc install (~40s/row): the classifier is node-builtins-only and target repos install their own deps.\n- First live CI validation passed on the pre-split draft (#189): all rows green, fresh-runner installs fine, matrix rows tracked by the status comment.","tree":{"sha":"4396454934fc4e7da2801582802a220cfef156c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/git/trees/4396454934fc4e7da2801582802a220cfef156c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/git/commits/299cdd03c6610ef0ebc9db549adedf539a1debf2","verification":{"payload":"tree 4396454934fc4e7da2801582802a220cfef156c8\nparent bb1cf7e66b60a8d318711215ffb70a07fbba11d0\nauthor Dunqing <dengqing0821@gmail.com> 1783613225 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783613225 +0800\n\nfeat: run pinned repo test suites against minified sources (#191)\n\nSecond half of the runtime-correctness work (stacked on the bundle diff oracle PR, which carries the shared `runtime-minify` subcommand): run real repos'' own test suites against their minified sources.\n\n## Repo suites (`Test Runtime (<name>)`, 5 matrix rows)\n\nThe set favors framework monorepos with huge suites — vue (3,607 tests), svelte (7,557), solid (482) — plus es-toolkit and zod (big TS libraries). Repos whose tests import built dist (vitest, astro) are structurally out of scope: the classifier''s `git checkout` restore can''t rebuild gitignored dist, so this oracle is src-alias repos only. Per row:\n\n1. **Checkout** the pinned repo (pins in [`runtime-repos.json`](./runtime-repos.json)) into `target-repo/`; the pin means the only variable is oxc itself.\n2. **Install** via `scripts/runtime-test.mjs install <name> target-repo` (per-entry quirks documented in `notes`).\n3. **Minify in place** with `runtime-minify` — filenames/extensions preserved, so minified JS inside a `.ts` file flows through vitest/jest transpilation untouched. Only shipped source is matched, never tests: original assertions run against minified implementation.\n4. **Classify** differentially:\n\n```\nrun suite on minified sources\n├─ green ──────────────────────────→ pass\n└─ red → rerun once\n   ├─ green ───────────────────────→ pass (flake absorbed)\n   └─ red → git checkout -- .  → run suite unminified\n      ├─ green → FAIL   ← real minifier/transformer bug\n      └─ red   → pass + ::warning::  (env/flake rot, not oxc)\n```\n\nA row can only fail when the identical tests on the identical machine pass unminified and fail minified — upstream breakage and flaky tests are structurally unable to produce a false red. TS repos route through `oxc_transformer` first, so the oracle also catches transformer runtime bugs. A weekly workflow (`bump-runtime-repos.yml`) re-pins repos whose HEAD baseline passes, via PR, so CI on the bump PR validates new pins minified before merge.\n\n## Notes\n\n- **It already caught a real upstream bug — in vite, not oxc**: vetting the vue entry produced 377 deterministic failures that initially looked like a mangler scope collision. Systematic follow-up exonerated oxc (697/697 references bind identically; plain Node runs the minified file) and pinned the real cause: vite''s `ssrTransform` doesn''t treat `switch` blocks as lexical scopes, so switch-case `let`s mis-scope and same-named import references are left un-rewritten. Fixed upstream in vitejs/vite#22893; the one file is `ignore`d with the full analysis in its `notes` (remove when the fix propagates to rolldown-vite). Cross-check: terser''s output triggers the same vite bug; esbuild/swc escape only by name-allocation luck.\n- Process rule encoded by that episode: a red verdict gets plain-node confirmation before blaming oxc — the suite''s own module-transform layer is part of the executed stack.\n- Runtime rows skip the monitor-oxc install (~40s/row): the classifier is node-builtins-only and target repos install their own deps.\n- First live CI validation passed on the pre-split draft (#189): all rows green, fresh-runner installs fine, matrix rows tracked by the status comment.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT8cpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU14QAF/4I30Lwpywk4Ep+7QZsMkI\n52wLI7BTSbjlOFuQaes5GipuMjMZnQQXo/WJ3bvZr4M0q7263by9MjQSlW0L8Izk\nEpNc0dCoknJJyHchhHo3BWX2AenwbAHtoQIQQFQC15tIdrp+j01OygfFdjTpns0g\nZqx8bJQlpoZDsZ9r0Gvh1FnCc96aAd4fmBAnKUBzaQwUm0bIP+qwyDL5NKkm1Crf\nvcCV4SfH+b549V+E+A4j7G4MyQm5eWwu5VuvB1806klFWlMVkWq0HBQoT2HgLY9K\nunD3qfau/cOnAyXU4qvYQny4AqHdgpDskQcOOM7kNrAjZbiR+U5z+CKvwywHUZwb\nzrqTu+p7d33EgXIp+1p7JzHN3arDM6JardhEPMkW/arWeoenhgoIlzaAmf5vNht6\npczKD4uxEvuyv0E9nuF5UygXcLaAdhQs2ziy3XqeoN+EEbV0j7jQFmEF4YwoKixR\nsaJ/a2BmtB1Q/qSnAzSb8zYDspIiOICX2GRX4RJRApFktKfCrvL6bHEe6NdpgtMe\nn3liYzeAHkkAY4QlFDPGKzqPfckQqyHb6KssdvWRYqonBsiQO4f/6KQarScVAQG7\n1/D0j110jQTPjARpAiKwCecqfRZR7VQfy3y4+VN46XZ9lvWRJ3K4VxhrHAV8kvrn\n0GiR4oN8daGHTNrcgip8\n=L0c5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-09T16:07:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commit/299cdd03c6610ef0ebc9db549adedf539a1debf2","node_id":"C_kwDOMEGZSNoAKDI5OWNkZDAzYzY2MTBlZjBlYmM5ZGI1NDlhZGVkZjUzOWExZGViZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commit/bb1cf7e66b60a8d318711215ffb70a07fbba11d0","sha":"bb1cf7e66b60a8d318711215ffb70a07fbba11d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commits/bb1cf7e66b60a8d318711215ffb70a07fbba11d0"}],"sha":"299cdd03c6610ef0ebc9db549adedf539a1debf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commits/299cdd03c6610ef0ebc9db549adedf539a1debf2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29533304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Dunqing","id":29533304,"login":"Dunqing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NTMzMzA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commits/bb1cf7e66b60a8d318711215ffb70a07fbba11d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T16:01:50Z","email":"dengqing0821@gmail.com","name":"Dunqing"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T16:01:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add uglify corpus differential oracle (#192)\n\nThird oracle, stacked on the bundle diff PR (shares only the `runtime-minify` subcommand): run UglifyJS''s `test/compress` corpus — thousands of tiny programs with observable runtime output — as a differential check against oxc main. esbuild has run this exact corpus in CI for years; swc vendors it.\n\n## How it works\n\n`scripts/uglify-corpus-test.mjs <clone>`:\n\n1. Parse the corpus''s case DSL (token-aware scanner, provably complete: every `expect_stdout`-bearing case in the pinned corpus is accounted for — 3,568/3,568) and extract each runnable case to a scratch tree.\n2. Minify the whole tree with **one** `runtime-minify` pass (standard full pipeline; per-case uglify options deliberately ignored, as esbuild does).\n3. Execute original and minified per case in fresh `vm` contexts (ported uglify sandbox semantics: captured stdout, `Function#toString` normalization, 5s timeout) and byte-diff.\n\n**Purely differential**: expected output is always derived by executing the original in-run — the corpus''s own `expect_stdout` strings are never trusted, so corpus age can''t cause false reds. Originals run twice as a determinism gate (nondeterministic case → warning + auto-skip). Failures are pre-minimized repros by construction.\n\nCurrent numbers at the pinned corpus: **4,263 cases → 3,331 compared, 107 skipped (each with a documented reason in [`uglify-corpus.json`](./uglify-corpus.json)), 825 structurally excluded** (no runnable output / need a module loader for lowered helper imports / node-version-gated). Runs in about a minute on system node with no installs.\n\n## It found 14 real oxc bug classes on its first run\n\nVetting surfaced 14 distinct deterministic bug classes across 54 cases (several reproduced in plain node), now in the skip list as documented defects pending upstream issues/fixes — highlights: `delete (0, NaN)` folded to `delete NaN` (flips `true`→`false`), strict directive lost when eliminating a strict IIFE (`this` becomes globalThis), `for (a => { a in a; }; ;)` rejected by the parser (no-`in` leaking into an arrow body), BigInt `**=` miscompiled into a throwing unary `+`, async-generator `try/finally` skipping the `finally`, lone-surrogate strings emitted lossily as U+FFFD, `with`-scope-shadowed globals substituted (`Infinity` → `1/0`), a mangler TDZ collision, and six more (arguments linkage, Annex-B hoisting, destructuring side-effect order, optional-chain `this`, unary-`+` timing, DCE dropping a throwing call). Upstream filing to follow separately; each skip entry references the local evidence trail.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The 121 module-loader exclusions (~3.6%) are lowered-helper `require()`s that can''t resolve in the builtins-only vm — an acknowledged coverage gap, deliberately traded for a zero-install CI row.\n- `record.needs` gains the job; the one-line union with the repo-suites PR''s `needs` resolves trivially at merge.","tree":{"sha":"3486f3294887c719b184cc4dbf4cf42b86d4bea7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/git/trees/3486f3294887c719b184cc4dbf4cf42b86d4bea7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/git/commits/bb1cf7e66b60a8d318711215ffb70a07fbba11d0","verification":{"payload":"tree 3486f3294887c719b184cc4dbf4cf42b86d4bea7\nparent 288e422d20e85a124e893792e2e41472468a70bf\nauthor Dunqing <dengqing0821@gmail.com> 1783612910 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783612910 +0800\n\nfeat: add uglify corpus differential oracle (#192)\n\nThird oracle, stacked on the bundle diff PR (shares only the `runtime-minify` subcommand): run UglifyJS''s `test/compress` corpus — thousands of tiny programs with observable runtime output — as a differential check against oxc main. esbuild has run this exact corpus in CI for years; swc vendors it.\n\n## How it works\n\n`scripts/uglify-corpus-test.mjs <clone>`:\n\n1. Parse the corpus''s case DSL (token-aware scanner, provably complete: every `expect_stdout`-bearing case in the pinned corpus is accounted for — 3,568/3,568) and extract each runnable case to a scratch tree.\n2. Minify the whole tree with **one** `runtime-minify` pass (standard full pipeline; per-case uglify options deliberately ignored, as esbuild does).\n3. Execute original and minified per case in fresh `vm` contexts (ported uglify sandbox semantics: captured stdout, `Function#toString` normalization, 5s timeout) and byte-diff.\n\n**Purely differential**: expected output is always derived by executing the original in-run — the corpus''s own `expect_stdout` strings are never trusted, so corpus age can''t cause false reds. Originals run twice as a determinism gate (nondeterministic case → warning + auto-skip). Failures are pre-minimized repros by construction.\n\nCurrent numbers at the pinned corpus: **4,263 cases → 3,331 compared, 107 skipped (each with a documented reason in [`uglify-corpus.json`](./uglify-corpus.json)), 825 structurally excluded** (no runnable output / need a module loader for lowered helper imports / node-version-gated). Runs in about a minute on system node with no installs.\n\n## It found 14 real oxc bug classes on its first run\n\nVetting surfaced 14 distinct deterministic bug classes across 54 cases (several reproduced in plain node), now in the skip list as documented defects pending upstream issues/fixes — highlights: `delete (0, NaN)` folded to `delete NaN` (flips `true`→`false`), strict directive lost when eliminating a strict IIFE (`this` becomes globalThis), `for (a => { a in a; }; ;)` rejected by the parser (no-`in` leaking into an arrow body), BigInt `**=` miscompiled into a throwing unary `+`, async-generator `try/finally` skipping the `finally`, lone-surrogate strings emitted lossily as U+FFFD, `with`-scope-shadowed globals substituted (`Infinity` → `1/0`), a mangler TDZ collision, and six more (arguments linkage, Annex-B hoisting, destructuring side-effect order, optional-chain `this`, unary-`+` timing, DCE dropping a throwing call). Upstream filing to follow separately; each skip entry references the local evidence trail.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The 121 module-loader exclusions (~3.6%) are lowered-helper `require()`s that can''t resolve in the builtins-only vm — an acknowledged coverage gap, deliberately traded for a zero-install CI row.\n- `record.needs` gains the job; the one-line union with the repo-suites PR''s `needs` resolves trivially at merge.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT8XuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAD20QAHGzDGUaQ7r6YVK7T+z01DDs\nr4iv8eTLOPMRUvPMe/5SUAPPHtqN7p1zMyb9m08pmPdN9WUxfqIEw/vm+k+V/FyA\nkboLytEl/KO1yuRcOQWyp9ukVu96wNwLjRs1Mnxq7wekRsNixmdfx/+gWYgV9FrQ\nxDyfjweskUSCjSYSzldglDSqFdnSjA4u2CmeLv/B86ejIagqnfQIFe8Fo0mYOoxJ\nEEBnN2JS2CXGRaGn7S8Kxxey8oLIs/H7WsUr32kCMZt1CHVihvjezm06nRxmNJAT\nsDtMwcIUpWKel0ruspDaBg4qvJuuyRPIZsaDTofCCv8k7j6vhtUw8QRnWREXV/3H\n9mj2WPpVpI/vMST13kmD1L9fdOd5izkQeQhgK8+sSv5E3WE/Pl7GXtyw/F7K7359\nx8H6/TCd98hv3cx212mvM87L7sDuVwMwZINj/sinc4tlhLjZCByjvuI0WZqfxMLQ\n4jpY0zu3olV0RmuPgpPGdTmKZt9eX9+WY/p1byFKsztnJy232b+jJvOAXdjRrHAR\nNV9IzVEI9ixT0xXdoNjN3OZf6yYLAHnb1LjY1bsi8XdCsSz3ToV1FThk1IZ1BowH\n8+g3HKF4qDPPTd/vZMb7o5BJGOkJyuG0NqpnYy62vzA9y10ESYzAQClwL0e0izZG\nBchUbb+Ai1xpErhaC8pq\n=yjRC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-09T16:01:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commit/bb1cf7e66b60a8d318711215ffb70a07fbba11d0","node_id":"C_kwDOMEGZSNoAKGJiMWNmN2U2NmI2MGE4ZDMxODcxMTIxNWZmYjcwYTA3ZmJiYTExZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commit/288e422d20e85a124e893792e2e41472468a70bf","sha":"288e422d20e85a124e893792e2e41472468a70bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commits/288e422d20e85a124e893792e2e41472468a70bf"}],"sha":"bb1cf7e66b60a8d318711215ffb70a07fbba11d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commits/bb1cf7e66b60a8d318711215ffb70a07fbba11d0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29533304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Dunqing","id":29533304,"login":"Dunqing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NTMzMzA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commits/288e422d20e85a124e893792e2e41472468a70bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T15:59:51Z","email":"dengqing0821@gmail.com","name":"Dunqing"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T15:59:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add bundle diff runtime oracle for the minifier (#190)\n\nAdds runtime **execution** coverage for the minifier: today''s oracles (idempotency + \"the package still imports\") never run minified code, so a semantically wrong compression that still parses goes undetected. This PR adds the shared `runtime-minify` infrastructure plus the **bundle diff oracle**; a stacked PR adds the repo-suites oracle on top.\n\n## `runtime-minify` subcommand (shared infra)\n\n`monitor-oxc runtime-minify --name <entry> --dir <dir> [--config <path>]` rewrites every file matching a config entry''s `sources` globs **in place, keeping the filename and extension**, through transform → compress → mangle → whitespace using the same `Driver` as the other suites. Both this PR''s oracle and the stacked repo-suites PR drive it.\n\n## Bundle diff oracle (`Test Runtime Bundles`)\n\nReal-world minifier input is mostly **bundled output** — giant single scopes with inlined imports. Production mega-bundles already sit in this repo''s node_modules, and a CLI tool''s output on fixed inputs is a deterministic oracle:\n\n```\nrun tool on committed fixtures      → expected output   (twice: determinism gate)\nminify the tool''s bundle in place   → runtime-minify (oxc main)\nrun tool again                      → actual output\nbyte-diff exit code + stdout/stderr + emitted files; restore bundle\n```\n\n16 entries in [`bundle-tools.json`](./bundle-tools.json): typescript (`_tsc.js`, 6.2MB single scope), webpack (645-file CJS at scale), sass (`sass.dart.js`), prettier, rollup, vite (rolldown-vite dist), vitest, jest (3 per-package entries so a red attributes to the specific minified package), babel (`@babel/standalone` 4.4MB + parser + core), vue-compiler-sfc, jiti, terser (minify-the-minified). Each entry''s `notes` records the load trace proving the minified files are the files the invocation executes. No pins and no baseline classifier — the expected output is generated in-run, so nothing external can cause a false red. The runner logs sizes each run (e.g. `webpack: raw 5,137,145 -> 1,860,989 bytes (-63.8%), gzip -52.2%`), doubling as a coarse size-regression signal.\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Mutation-tested**: two deliberate bugs injected into a local oxc checkout were both caught — a `??`→`||` compressor bug fired 2/16 entries (sass exit-code change, babel-standalone `TypeError`); a mangler `base54` name collision fired 15/16 (typescript: `Identifier ''ye'' has already been declared`). No false positives.\n- `vitest` and `@babel/standalone` are added to `dependencies` (not the generated `devDependencies`) so `generate.mjs` regeneration preserves them; the smoke-test lists are generated independently, so they''re never bare-imported.\n- On failure the minified bundles + expected/actual outputs upload as a CI artifact.\n- Planned follow-up phases: UglifyJS `expect_stdout` corpus, cargo-patched-rolldown daily job (real vite pipeline on oxc main), seeded differential fuzzing.","tree":{"sha":"0e1282da8cdfa480d8af1f8b9db19214cc4461f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/git/trees/0e1282da8cdfa480d8af1f8b9db19214cc4461f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/git/commits/288e422d20e85a124e893792e2e41472468a70bf","verification":{"payload":"tree 0e1282da8cdfa480d8af1f8b9db19214cc4461f0\nparent 6809fbd8285741b69aea386cf3f8c540e831bde7\nauthor Dunqing <dengqing0821@gmail.com> 1783612791 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783612791 +0800\n\nfeat: add bundle diff runtime oracle for the minifier (#190)\n\nAdds runtime **execution** coverage for the minifier: today''s oracles (idempotency + \"the package still imports\") never run minified code, so a semantically wrong compression that still parses goes undetected. This PR adds the shared `runtime-minify` infrastructure plus the **bundle diff oracle**; a stacked PR adds the repo-suites oracle on top.\n\n## `runtime-minify` subcommand (shared infra)\n\n`monitor-oxc runtime-minify --name <entry> --dir <dir> [--config <path>]` rewrites every file matching a config entry''s `sources` globs **in place, keeping the filename and extension**, through transform → compress → mangle → whitespace using the same `Driver` as the other suites. Both this PR''s oracle and the stacked repo-suites PR drive it.\n\n## Bundle diff oracle (`Test Runtime Bundles`)\n\nReal-world minifier input is mostly **bundled output** — giant single scopes with inlined imports. Production mega-bundles already sit in this repo''s node_modules, and a CLI tool''s output on fixed inputs is a deterministic oracle:\n\n```\nrun tool on committed fixtures      → expected output   (twice: determinism gate)\nminify the tool''s bundle in place   → runtime-minify (oxc main)\nrun tool again                      → actual output\nbyte-diff exit code + stdout/stderr + emitted files; restore bundle\n```\n\n16 entries in [`bundle-tools.json`](./bundle-tools.json): typescript (`_tsc.js`, 6.2MB single scope), webpack (645-file CJS at scale), sass (`sass.dart.js`), prettier, rollup, vite (rolldown-vite dist), vitest, jest (3 per-package entries so a red attributes to the specific minified package), babel (`@babel/standalone` 4.4MB + parser + core), vue-compiler-sfc, jiti, terser (minify-the-minified). Each entry''s `notes` records the load trace proving the minified files are the files the invocation executes. No pins and no baseline classifier — the expected output is generated in-run, so nothing external can cause a false red. The runner logs sizes each run (e.g. `webpack: raw 5,137,145 -> 1,860,989 bytes (-63.8%), gzip -52.2%`), doubling as a coarse size-regression signal.\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Mutation-tested**: two deliberate bugs injected into a local oxc checkout were both caught — a `??`→`||` compressor bug fired 2/16 entries (sass exit-code change, babel-standalone `TypeError`); a mangler `base54` name collision fired 15/16 (typescript: `Identifier ''ye'' has already been declared`). No false positives.\n- `vitest` and `@babel/standalone` are added to `dependencies` (not the generated `devDependencies`) so `generate.mjs` regeneration preserves them; the smoke-test lists are generated independently, so they''re never bare-imported.\n- On failure the minified bundles + expected/actual outputs upload as a CI artifact.\n- Planned follow-up phases: UglifyJS `expect_stdout` corpus, cargo-patched-rolldown daily job (real vite pipeline on oxc main), seeded differential fuzzing.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT8V3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArGoQAASMetKhKokkqG5r99dUNMvx\n8Ffk6VXWA5bIYadeULxcx3jhJYqwfF0Zcv5IanE6atEoOfXwHpSOjOCKmAwY3ROJ\nfX6eukkPXurDZ8OSJ4rvUIAU4g351KEb5Ojr9uBW+1vwtgzCm6HsCKsjOnlCN1ny\nK6SvP1msOpJ7macS1lNpHrA9AHnci3LhCw99gZhjsN32mImywj54OKxkTlqNwKNr\nRHtKgqfu2hbZvx+Wx2WUrAwEbKjhJ8oQ+Wpo/HjcErc4AKs+MrWRkKoT9xOQ+wIZ\nMqqK/Gy5+cn/SGXChRHNWVaB3swi8iDYMl4miooYu4ewHQ7IdczI6pGcYEXsSRbI\nElcAlHKxxr0WZfCRRXDkgjZ+s28DzIeBaS4JWOfo6E3XTtpcLWWxr2CncbHxH76q\npYzntRSX7HFWADYudMY4klsvzZfNtwW+xRBqMCDNMeCEbmpXO42343IZJFn2XXFs\n8/uM+IRzYq65vX8HpeTPNZAZCQYSosiLGfNXYNIQzmjnu2PydUv2AIbeWNKqEfAm\nS2UkedHn2dkGdh859v/ekwmqOaPXuYobaYsQI0XVygkj6rOf3HH2+nOJNTIw6AUG\nbu6EMOV/dqUIlAwdtArUaO6L/0jR8SVNE9pUMV+Ipfm3tyW20znI/gLa5FqwiV7W\nt8iR6NFbEE+4pq3P//eZ\n=Hw8f\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-09T15:59:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1986444