24cf18a","sha":"efcbc1a098fbfa8d0800cf7369678f5f224cf18a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commits/efcbc1a098fbfa8d0800cf7369678f5f224cf18a"}],"sha":"659fcb194ff2989a5cb59948b0819b9eb72bad4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commits/659fcb194ff2989a5cb59948b0819b9eb72bad4d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29533304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Dunqing","id":29533304,"login":"Dunqing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NTMzMzA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commits/efcbc1a098fbfa8d0800cf7369678f5f224cf18a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T13:50:43Z","email":"dengqing0821@gmail.com","name":"Dunqing"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T13:50:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(driver): use CompressOptions::dce() for the dce runner (#167)\n\n## Summary\n\n`Driver::dce` was calling `Compressor::dead_code_elimination` with\n`CompressOptions::default()`. That default is\n`CompressOptions::smallest()` — full minify, including `sequences: true`\nand `join_vars: true` — not DCE. So the \"dce\" runner has been a\nfull-minify runner for a while; `oxc_minifier --example dce` uses\n`CompressOptions::dce()` (no sequences/join-vars) for the same job.\n\nTwo consequences of the misalignment:\n\n- The `if (...) { throw X; }` → `if (...) throw X` and `new Error(...)`\nternary rewrites shift comment ownership across the inserted parens, so\nthe runner''s idempotency check (one pass vs two) trips on roughly 650\nfiles where the second pass repositions the comments differently from\nthe first. See the `micromark-core-commonmark` / `jest-each` / `aws-sdk`\nfailures in run\n[26082752217](https://github.com/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/actions/runs/26082752217/job/76688477774).\n- The `dce` label is misleading; the mangler/compressor runners already\ncover full-minify behaviour.\n\nSwitching to `CompressOptions::dce()` clears those ~650 failures without\nlosing DCE coverage. Verified locally on the full 116,429-file corpus:\n759 → 9 idempotency failures, the remaining 9 being two distinct\nupstream oxc bugs (`/* @__PURE__ */` not re-evaluated after peephole\ninlining, and arrow-alternate comment-attachment loss) that need\nseparate fixes.","tree":{"sha":"99c6a4a21606c8f147d45c55093dde324ce96d10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/git/trees/99c6a4a21606c8f147d45c55093dde324ce96d10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/git/commits/efcbc1a098fbfa8d0800cf7369678f5f224cf18a","verification":{"payload":"tree 99c6a4a21606c8f147d45c55093dde324ce96d10\nparent 2f2b22c534b6259699183f9acd346178ed2ce147\nauthor Dunqing <dengqing0821@gmail.com> 1779198643 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779198643 +0800\n\nfix(driver): use CompressOptions::dce() for the dce runner (#167)\n\n## Summary\n\n`Driver::dce` was calling `Compressor::dead_code_elimination` with\n`CompressOptions::default()`. That default is\n`CompressOptions::smallest()` — full minify, including `sequences: true`\nand `join_vars: true` — not DCE. So the \"dce\" runner has been a\nfull-minify runner for a while; `oxc_minifier --example dce` uses\n`CompressOptions::dce()` (no sequences/join-vars) for the same job.\n\nTwo consequences of the misalignment:\n\n- The `if (...) { throw X; }` → `if (...) throw X` and `new Error(...)`\nternary rewrites shift comment ownership across the inserted parens, so\nthe runner''s idempotency check (one pass vs two) trips on roughly 650\nfiles where the second pass repositions the comments differently from\nthe first. See the `micromark-core-commonmark` / `jest-each` / `aws-sdk`\nfailures in run\n[26082752217](https://github.com/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/actions/runs/26082752217/job/76688477774).\n- The `dce` label is misleading; the mangler/compressor runners already\ncover full-minify behaviour.\n\nSwitching to `CompressOptions::dce()` clears those ~650 failures without\nlosing DCE coverage. Verified locally on the full 116,429-file corpus:\n759 → 9 idempotency failures, the remaining 9 being two distinct\nupstream oxc bugs (`/* @__PURE__ */` not re-evaluated after peephole\ninlining, and arrow-alternate comment-attachment loss) that need\nseparate fixes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDGqzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU+sQAD3zBJYOf5fUCIeuV60AyX+o\n4FL8iuYoOK1lzZaAagFT4r8rqGAQi11O0Ps0DKerVKhLg9GycVyAeudIdWM+0EQm\nHWgDNKNN4vKAJ3ihdpSTRCVPgMeoWaHP9tG9iiiyr/0EzXEiviWeaXuHzcSFekBV\nQkUMzKmmQ9YhHBZNeJpx5ph84W/Wq5+3kei/n1SimzoC9HN82SfuE+C/CjfcLLlJ\n3OVAz7r2ZHUPpV3Ow3297Qsxk6JT8+94OV4um6bISC3d+iV7Onnt5U6kMtea3w+2\ndHokWWyihiNDf5oPMXuWz08W0NJdmmvnvHpgWOij51NI6+L0g7hDmqEiU52TywwW\nfJbZJQLDp1o2Qc8WxukPbvbzcI3eosS2E9rr4MCb+oKj0KqnEzX3RIqw4Ohcp1HG\n5YQ2/2a9zQT4bfjW/XbRac3OwGrL0IBuLvjvMj/vN3iYrSX5Q5hmY1vBb8jycqbM\n3L+jgK9Eob7AUD14jIb2z2HCrCFKUZ82julT0718FFO+n52k55430O65leXqfJBY\nGC8svJHn90iyo7n5qOFuhkUyIvVZW7qR+4bAKl70ACdM/sQquO/pRuQ0bcG8Z6sn\n6E2ek3PCsWtuGctMxAgSevyr85zPAr+ZpsxRf5dPMG72VD12mZJognSgtkvKajhz\nFBQOUS+cD2IjbZLp56vt\n=8keq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-19T13:50:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":