_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commits/21162636ffecaafbde6030f91e75b07c2dc9f4c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-26T14:37:33Z","email":"dengqing0821@gmail.com","name":"Dunqing"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-26T14:37:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: avoid clobbering shipped JS files during transformer test (#159)\n\n## Summary\n- Some packages ship TS sources beside compiled JS. The transformer test\nwas unconditionally writing the transformed output to the `.js` path,\nclobbering the original shipped JS entry used by the runtime import\ntest.\n- Added a guard to skip writing when a JS counterpart already exists on\ndisk.\n\n## Test plan\n- [ ] Verify `cargo check` passes\n- [ ] Run the monitor against a package that ships both `.ts` and `.js`\nfiles and confirm the shipped JS is preserved\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b77eeb9475c0f3f7409b4e81688a2791cf9b728f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/git/trees/b77eeb9475c0f3f7409b4e81688a2791cf9b728f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/git/commits/21162636ffecaafbde6030f91e75b07c2dc9f4c6","verification":{"payload":"tree b77eeb9475c0f3f7409b4e81688a2791cf9b728f\nparent 768406b2d9fb7015fe481a7ceabddbb6c360469c\nauthor Dunqing <dengqing0821@gmail.com> 1777214253 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777214253 +0800\n\nfix: avoid clobbering shipped JS files during transformer test (#159)\n\n## Summary\n- Some packages ship TS sources beside compiled JS. The transformer test\nwas unconditionally writing the transformed output to the `.js` path,\nclobbering the original shipped JS entry used by the runtime import\ntest.\n- Added a guard to skip writing when a JS counterpart already exists on\ndisk.\n\n## Test plan\n- [ ] Verify `cargo check` passes\n- [ ] Run the monitor against a package that ships both `.ts` and `.js`\nfiles and confirm the shipped JS is preserved\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp7iMtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4MAQALCgurVHuSF3O4cHDJNzRm8J\nrs4U/RL7caN6yeY4c5qJpY8HWqAguEfx84A8OUWdvZjXkiGrYFHz2dWkGMxIxMxx\nBMnNiAgAY4hhKrM/p/YpHz+6M4Y/lLVBSf2im8JpP7+dSA6SeZEv3+7Haa98zJvh\nO05KG1O00VgLmDJzCbTKmfsjR6aNFlsoKkgGq0K1276cdlAMTBmJ0kga4eqaALn/\n/+s7MgtEOGvR6+W19y0mtkczynSUOnqblSVwnb1ZHOTGno6595vbsOPLu5scSQjI\nUeGEGnwlFjSZ+XheYOiKaQ3tQ1JVKS3rOy2NqmJ6jKs2/qy/qo/d4528SBOwisbg\nP98hpA/nGWC3MdIN4F58s67V711ss6VlGLH7CEuOdT9dflXY6GCQY8qRcRQBPLCp\ncDD3x6EUgWajAsp3s0S3jDDHPI9Zjd8fD2Owj3G8ewWzpzvNzcN0lyoiVuEUQtp2\n8ZfaenhqNDleZWJ0W1Hh1zxle38WtizbwwgllZRqH7nDIZlB5P+3JjwglmzBWtYE\n++F2JsaLp4Rt2wFMPmsOAfu23jdZ4ZlNuDMz5T5BleliFbw4DXHVCjx6VUmiRFn1\n3bGQ7XZnuREHCWFPc2A8ZTaa8I011/M8RV3Q3UIUV2O6oDAbbw+Uf2LVAOFR7Ad3\nefBvI4v+P8k3dpozJb4o\n=7Mus\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-26T14:37:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commit/21162636ffecaafbde6030f91e75b07c2dc9f4c6","node_id":"C_kwDOMEGZSNoAKDIxMTYyNjM2ZmZlY2FhZmJkZTYwMzBmOTFlNzViMDdjMmRjOWY0YzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commit/768406b2d9fb7015fe481a7ceabddbb6c360469c","sha":"768406b2d9fb7015fe481a7ceabddbb6c360469c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commits/768406b2d9fb7015fe481a7ceabddbb6c360469c"}],"sha":"21162636ffecaafbde6030f91e75b07c2dc9f4c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commits/21162636ffecaafbde6030f91e75b07c2dc9f4c6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29533304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Dunqing","id":29533304,"login":"Dunqing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NTMzMzA0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dunqing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/commits/768406b2d9fb7015fe481a7ceabddbb6c360469c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-23T12:32:15Z","email":"dengqing0821@gmail.com","name":"Dunqing"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-23T12:32:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: stabilize monitor smoke test imports (#157)\n\n## What changed\n- add `@oxc-project/runtime` as a root dependency\n- add the matching lockfile entries so transformer smoke tests can\nresolve injected Oxc helpers\n- keep `eslint-plugin-jest` and `jquery` in the generated smoke tests as\ndocumented expected-failure cases\n- generate `assert.rejects(...)` coverage for those two baseline-broken\nimports in both dynamic and static smoke tests\n\n## Why this changed\nThe original transformer failure came from transformed package output\nimporting `@oxc-project/runtime` while the monitor harness did not\ninstall that runtime.\n\nAfter fixing that, CI exposed two separate baseline package issues in\nthe generated top-level import smoke tests:\n- `eslint-plugin-jest` currently pulls an `@typescript-eslint/utils`\npath that crashes against the resolved ESLint 10 package set\n- `jquery@4` throws on plain Node.js import because it requires a window\nwith a document\n\nThese are not Oxc transform regressions, but they are real behavior in\nthe current dependency graph, so the monitor should record them\nexplicitly instead of skipping them or treating them as unexpected\ntransformer failures.\n\n## Impact\n- transformed packages can resolve Oxc helper imports during runtime\nsmoke tests\n- known baseline-broken packages remain installed and exercised in the\nsmoke-test matrix\n- future regenerations preserve those expected-failure assertions via\n`generate.mjs`\n\n## Root cause\n- `@adobe/css-tools` itself does not publish an `@oxc-project/runtime`\nimport; that import is introduced by the transform pass, so the missing\nruntime was a harness dependency gap\n- `eslint-plugin-jest` failure is upstream package incompatibility in\nthe current `latest` dependency graph, not a transform bug\n- `jquery` failure is a direct Node runtime incompatibility for plain\nimport, not a transform bug\n\n## Validation\n- `git diff --check`\n- `node --check generate.mjs`\n- `node --check src/dynamic.test.mjs`\n- `node --check src/static.test.mjs`\n- minimal standalone repro for `@typescript-eslint/utils` /\n`eslint-plugin-jest` against ESLint 10\n- minimal standalone repro for `jquery@4` on plain Node import\n- full monitor suite not executed locally in this checkout","tree":{"sha":"611dc536f0a5af7831550df3cc07cdd47717fd5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/git/trees/611dc536f0a5af7831550df3cc07cdd47717fd5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/oxc-project/monitor-oxc/git/commits/768406b2d9fb7015fe481a7ceabddbb6c360469c","verification":{"payload":"tree 611dc536f0a5af7831550df3cc07cdd47717fd5d\nparent 29b246a127835408f95ec3dc24d32dcb45974238\nauthor Dunqing <dengqing0821@gmail.com> 1776947535 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776947535 +0800\n\nchore: stabilize monitor smoke test imports (#157)\n\n## What changed\n- add `@oxc-project/runtime` as a root dependency\n- add the matching lockfile entries so transformer smoke tests can\nresolve injected Oxc helpers\n- keep `eslint-plugin-jest` and `jquery` in the generated smoke tests as\ndocumented expected-failure cases\n- generate `assert.rejects(...)` coverage for those two baseline-broken\nimports in both dynamic and static smoke tests\n\n## Why this changed\nThe original transformer failure came from transformed package output\nimporting `@oxc-project/runtime` while the monitor harness did not\ninstall that runtime.\n\nAfter fixing that, CI exposed two separate baseline package issues in\nthe generated top-level import smoke tests:\n- `eslint-plugin-jest` currently pulls an `@typescript-eslint/utils`\npath that crashes against the resolved ESLint 10 package set\n- `jquery@4` throws on plain Node.js import because it requires a window\nwith a document\n\nThese are not Oxc transform regressions, but they are real behavior in\nthe current dependency graph, so the monitor should record them\nexplicitly instead of skipping them or treating them as unexpected\ntransformer failures.\n\n## Impact\n- transformed packages can resolve Oxc helper imports during runtime\nsmoke tests\n- known baseline-broken packages remain installed and exercised in the\nsmoke-test matrix\n- future regenerations preserve those expected-failure assertions via\n`generate.mjs`\n\n## Root cause\n- `@adobe/css-tools` itself does not publish an `@oxc-project/runtime`\nimport; that import is introduced by the transform pass, so the missing\nruntime was a harness dependency gap\n- `eslint-plugin-jest` failure is upstream package incompatibility in\nthe current `latest` dependency graph, not a transform bug\n- `jquery` failure is a direct Node runtime incompatibility for plain\nimport, not a transform bug\n\n## Validation\n- `git diff --check`\n- `node --check generate.mjs`\n- `node --check src/dynamic.test.mjs`\n- `node --check src/static.test.mjs`\n- minimal standalone repro for `@typescript-eslint/utils` /\n`eslint-plugin-jest` against ESLint 10\n- minimal standalone repro for `jquery@4` on plain Node import\n- full monitor suite not executed locally in this checkout","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp6hFPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnnMQAGGu8ZWVUCjct4QYtRwMeZr9\ndkIzVaXxjJjmgN//9DODZc375QK+qw90A9r3i4ipvXRBCF0DxGE1PyBgr41OYnF5\nTbegBFcLNHT+9GbL4WIEezGVRYAeLla+qgevyaeUjawC395JtyKAfX0UjcNeLn7O\njmU04/FfbmUukHAOzA9C2vz3bNWrRIvmGQAGsFZpNEgKv4jE3v5EtB751GiheOh5\nJbsG2aBJRuZz9Za0THpj3eP9LN9gJOTp4FlwCCGb3eLS3n2i15ZNCU0b9doakLbr\nysMaPgg7oz+pNP2m62odzdjVdT0CpBJif8vFDZFbSTd/y7SOOr/F0kmGzE7VmzMj\nBJqULqBQ9fMjoGARvdCdUKfLbUhwij5r2fi7LDSa+Lhov/fFiltRRFWiFVhC8M+k\nuX1GJf7K7aF3gV56FdCbtqILuNS9z1rDlr7Xa/CprBtLA3uqVqLyhdg6axTLBurW\nyAJ/gIcGQCmaFHykSympEflVBaiheM+F2D1liSo9SFPHYwZ63iqtZBjzeqnDbOIa\nnXpjVxIt1Svk9b5ncqy1zgBRhyOb1GKDklfbx8Xkj5ZD6IBq3ikX+Ga48o2oTM9F\n/e9i4cvFkYQRw/nTOvs//0zbNCuPp4P