"id":137657032,"login":"dcblakesleyWss","node_id":"U_kgDOCDR6yA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesleyWss/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesleyWss/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesleyWss/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesleyWss/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesleyWss/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesleyWss","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/5dc1280028a2da3c43774903c4262eb7d1dd1269/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T20:39:40Z","email":"dblakesley@webstaurantstore.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T20:39:40Z","email":"dblakesley@webstaurantstore.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"Cut 10.8.4: FormOptions.IdPrefix\n\nBumps both AssemblyVersions to 10.8.4 and documents the one feature that\nlanded since 10.8.3 — the form-wide id prefix and its FormDefaults\ncounterpart — in the README''s FormDefaults section plus a changelog entry.\n\nAlso finishes the feature''s empty-string handling: ResolveIdPrefix now\ntreats an empty FormOptions.IdPrefix as unset, so a consumer''s unset string\nvariable falls through to FormDefaults instead of silently blocking it —\nmatching the empty-string guards AttributesHelper.GetId already applies at\nevery other id layer. Covered by a new EditControlInitTests fact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"858c3f02991332ca1da9aa0c87299b519398f692","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/858c3f02991332ca1da9aa0c87299b519398f692"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/5dc1280028a2da3c43774903c4262eb7d1dd1269","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,