ter and DisplayFormat honoring already ship\nand only an opt-in preset plus DataType(Currency) are proposed.\n\nImplementation deferred; the option-independent a11y remediation already landed\nseparately and is listed so it is not re-planned.","tree":{"sha":"f5bae3f61e9e6efd7b959918503f59784a401073","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/f5bae3f61e9e6efd7b959918503f59784a401073"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/e637938b40eddc2e6885ffca653f3891c09753fb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/e637938b40eddc2e6885ffca653f3891c09753fb","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKGU2Mzc5MzhiNDBlZGRjMmU2ODg1ZmZjYTY1M2YzODkxYzA5NzUzZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/eda0288984b0cc2e3784e8cbe1be85964d4d8296","sha":"eda0288984b0cc2e3784e8cbe1be85964d4d8296","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/eda0288984b0cc2e3784e8cbe1be85964d4d8296"}],"sha":"e637938b40eddc2e6885ffca653f3891c09753fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/e637938b40eddc2e6885ffca653f3891c09753fb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/eda0288984b0cc2e3784e8cbe1be85964d4d8296/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:54:47Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:54:47Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"README: the new OnSaveFailed args, the re-arm, and the Other-field rules\n\nDocuments FormAutoSaveFailureEventArgs and what happens to a failed save''s\nfields, the validation-state re-attempt, TimeProvider being read once, and\nthe fact that the after-the-validator placement only matters at\nDebounceMilliseconds 0. On the radio side: do not put a plain [Required]\non the OtherValue property, and the registration follows what renders.","tree":{"sha":"ad466ddc054fc168a093be2ed8dd52b56b0a1ffe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/ad466ddc054fc168a093be2ed8dd52b56b0a1ffe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/eda0288984b0cc2e3784e8cbe1be85964d4d8296","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/eda0288984b0cc2e3784e8cbe1be85964d4d8296","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKGVkYTAyODg5ODRiMGNjMmUzNzg0ZThjYmUxYmU4NTk2NGQ0ZDgyOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/ea83f894483b09caf00f5c687f0043d99c02d8f6","sha":"ea83f894483b09caf00f5c687f0043d99c02d8f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/ea83f894483b09caf00f5c687f0043d99c02d8f6"}],"sha":"eda0288984b0cc2e3784e8cbe1be85964d4d8296","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/eda0288984b0cc2e3784e8cbe1be85964d4d8296"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/ea83f894483b09caf00f5c687f0043d99c02d8f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:54:47Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:54:47Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"EditRadioEnum: the Other field registers only where it renders\n\nSyncOtherFieldRegistration was gated on _otherFieldBound alone, but the\nRadioOtherInput carrying id other-{id} renders only inside the markup''s\nShowEditor and HasOtherOption conditions -- both runtime-variable. With\nHasOtherOption off, or with FormOptions.IsEditMode false, FieldIds still\nsaid other-Priority while zero elements carried that id, so ValidationView\nemitted href pointing at nothing.\n\nThe anchor now tracks what renders, and re-syncs every parameter cycle:\nread-only MOVES the field onto the read-only element (which shows the\n\"Other: text\" form under the control''s own id) rather than dropping it,\nmatching what EditDateRange does for its End field and why the primary\nfield survives read-only; HasOtherOption off unregisters, since nothing\nrepresents the property then. Re-registration is same-owner, never\nunregister-first, per SyncResolvedId''s convention. Dispose unregisters\nonly what was actually registered -- otherwise it would drop another\ncontrol''s entry for the same property.\n\nNot gated on ShouldShowComponent(): a HidingMode-hidden control renders no\nelement for either field, and the primary registration stays put through\nthat too.\n\nAlso documents the interaction a plain [Required] on the OtherValue\nproperty has with the notification this control now raises: the validator\nruns against the null written on a switch away from Other, so the message\nsticks while a non-Other option is selected and gates FormAutoSave''s\ndefault SaveWhenInvalid=false. That property is conditionally required and\nshould be expressed as such.\n\nTests: the two dead-link shapes, both runtime flips, and the documented\n\"notification follows ValueChanged, never precedes it\" ordering, which\nnothing pinned.","tree":{"sha":"82b68545d6a90e3f9bc7bd98a659af5ec9e7ebe1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/82b68545d6a90e3f9bc7bd98a659af5ec9e7ebe1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/ea83f894483b09caf00f5c687f0043d99c02d8f6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/ea83f894483b09caf00f5c687f0043d99c02d8f6","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKGVhODNmODk0NDgzYjA5Y2FmMDBmNWM2ODdmMDA0M2Q5OWMwMmQ4ZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/6d87a324a606e592b77e98859ed725d95c74e8ce","sha":"6d87a324a606e592b77e98859ed725d95c74e8ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/6d87a324a606e592b77e98859ed725d95c74e8ce"}],"sha":"ea83f894483b09caf00f5c687f0043d99c02d8f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/ea83f894483b09caf00f5c687f0043d99c02d8f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/6d87a324a606e592b77e98859ed725d95c74e8ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:54:32Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:54:32Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"FormAutoSave: a failed save keeps its fields, and a gated skip re-arms\n\nFour defects in one component, all in the same file.\n\nA failed save silently dropped everything it was carrying. FlushAsync\nsnapshots the pending fields, clears them, and only then awaits the save;\nInvokeSaveAsync caught and returned normally, so a transient 503 while\nediting Age meant Age never appeared in any later ChangedFields again.\nA consumer PATCHing by ChangedFields -- the entire reason that list\nexists -- silently never persisted it. On failure the carried fields now\ngo BACK to the front of the pending set (they changed first, and\nChangedFields is first-seen order), de-duplicated against whatever\narrived during the save. Same for a failing coalesced trailing run.\n\nOnSaveFailed now carries them too: EventCallback<Exception> becomes\nEventCallback<FormAutoSaveFailureEventArgs>, a record of the context, the\nexception and the fields the failed save was handed -- what a consumer\nneeds to compensate when the retry is not the answer. Unreleased\ncomponent, so no compatibility shim.\n\nA validity-gated skip could permanently jam auto-save. The skip was\nterminal: nothing re-attempted it until another field changed, so a\nproperty that stays invalid (a conditionally-required one the user cannot\nfill) gated off the whole form, and messages cleared externally -- a\nserver-side ValidationMessageStore clear plus NotifyValidationStateChanged,\nwhich this library supports via RequiredResolver/FluentValidation --\nreleased nothing. The component now also subscribes to\nOnValidationStateChanged and re-attempts the skip when the form is valid\nagain, going back through the debounce rather than flushing on the spot so\nthe keystroke that fixed the field lands in the same save. Scoped to a\nskip that actually happened, and left alone while a save is in flight, so\nthe constant validation churn of typing costs one flag read and a save\nthat raises validation state cannot restart itself. The gate is also\nchecked before the trailing flag is cleared, so a skip no longer spends\nthe queued trailing run.\n\nA throwing OnSaveFailed was itself swallowed, contradicting the doc right\nabove it: it escaped into the discarded flush task and surfaced nowhere.\nIt is now dispatched, together with the save failure it was handling, and\nthe flush task is observed rather than dropped.\n\n_disposed is written on the dispatcher and read off it (the timer callback\nreads it before marshalling), so it is volatile now and the\n\"single-threaded by construction\" comment says so.\n\nDocs, no behavior change: TimeProvider is latched at first timer creation;\nthe after-the-validator placement only bites at DebounceMilliseconds 0;\nthe EditContext-swap branch is unreachable from a real EditForm.\n\nTests: 10 new (3 of them fail without the carry-forward, 1 without the\nre-arm), and the two that could not distinguish what they claimed are\nfixed -- the failure test now uses two different fields, and \"renders\nnothing\" compares the form''s markup with and without the component\ninstead of asserting an empty form that had no fields in it.","tree":{"sha":"335f876234dc0c5d304b08e0779234c2703f186b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/335f876234dc0c5d304b08e0779234c2703f186b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/6d87a324a606e592b77e98859ed725d95c74e8ce","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/6d87a324a606e592b77e98859ed725d95c74e8ce","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKDZkODdhMzI0YTYwNmU1OTJiNzdlOTg4NTllZDcyNWQ5NWM3NGU4Y2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/7d452a394eaa1ad23efeb1a3a50afb0b047b0810","sha":"7d452a394eaa1ad23efeb1a3a50afb0b047b0810","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/7d452a394eaa1ad23efeb1a3a50afb0b047b0810"}],"sha":"6d87a324a606e592b77e98859ed725d95c74e8ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/6d87a324a606e592b77e98859ed725d95c74e8ce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/7d452a394eaa1ad23efeb1a3a50afb0b047b0810/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:22:08Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:22:08Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"ToastQueue: read the token before publishing the source\n\nStartTimer put the CancellationTokenSource into _timers and only then read\ncts.Token. The instant it is published another thread can claim it\n(Pause/Remove/Clear/Dispose all TryRemove), Cancel it and Dispose it -- and\nCancellationTokenSource.Token throws ObjectDisposedException after disposal,\nstraight out of the caller''s Pause/Resume. That is the intermittent\nObjectDisposedException seen once from\nConcurrent_Pause_and_Resume_calls_on_the_same_id_never_throw.\n\nCapturing the token first closes it: Cancel always precedes Dispose here,\nso the worst case is an already-cancelled token, which Task.Delay honors\nwithout touching the disposed source. RemoveAfterAsync now also swallows\nOperationCanceledException (the base of TaskCanceledException) and a\nlate ObjectDisposedException rather than faulting a fire-and-forget task.","tree":{"sha":"bd2b0e403f72b509787d63401b95a34d6a640d87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/bd2b0e403f72b509787d63401b95a34d6a640d87"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/7d452a394eaa1ad23efeb1a3a50afb0b047b0810","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/7d452a394eaa1ad23efeb1a3a50afb0b047b0810","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKDdkNDUyYTM5NGVhYTFhZDIzZWZlYjFhM2E1MGFmYjBiMDQ3YjA4MTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/7a615a944e413ce35ff2ae09b16b5d8d436be581","sha":"7a615a944e413ce35ff2ae09b16b5d8d436be581","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/7a615a944e413ce35ff2ae09b16b5d8d436be581"}],"sha":"7d452a394eaa1ad23efeb1a3a50afb0b047b0810","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/7d452a394eaa1ad23efeb1a3a50afb0b047b0810"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/7a615a944e413ce35ff2ae09b16b5d8d436be581/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:20:19Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:20:19Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"README: correct the FocusFirstField skip list, marker cost, and caveats\n\n- The skip list now matches what the resolver does: aria-disabled counts as\n  disabled, and a readonly element that declares aria-readonly=\"false\" is a\n  candidate.\n- The <template> markers'' CSS cost was understated. Measured: the end\n  marker IS the last child so :last-child breaks, the parent stops matching\n  :empty, +/~ sibling combinators shift, and tbody > tr:nth-child(odd)\n  zebra striping breaks (:nth-of-type does not). Flex/grid and the\n  library''s own positional selectors are unaffected -- worth stating too.\n- Documents the bounded retry for asynchronous forms, plus the\n  deterministic alternative (put the scope inside the @if).\n- Three previously undocumented consequences: flipping FocusFirstField true\n  after first render is a permanent no-op; an app-root true silently arms\n  every nested FormDefaults; and the outer of two scopes rendering in one\n  batch wins.\n- The dialog paragraph no longer overstates the ordering: the overlay now\n  offers the open to an armed scope, so first open and reopen are both a\n  single move.","tree":{"sha":"c96440bde6d5ce0256fd7917c8c69514d152570b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/c96440bde6d5ce0256fd7917c8c69514d152570b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/7a615a944e413ce35ff2ae09b16b5d8d436be581","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/7a615a944e413ce35ff2ae09b16b5d8d436be581","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKDdhNjE1YTk0NGU0MTNjZTM1ZmYyYWUwOWIxNmI1ZDhkNDM2YmU1ODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/9c030cb53e313d43512d1e8a932c59fb9d11b31f","sha":"9c030cb53e313d43512d1e8a932c59fb9d11b31f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/9c030cb53e313d43512d1e8a932c59fb9d11b31f"}],"sha":"7a615a944e413ce35ff2ae09b16b5d8d436be581","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/7a615a944e413ce35ff2ae09b16b5d8d436be581"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/9c030cb53e313d43512d1e8a932c59fb9d11b31f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:18:19Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:18:19Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"FocusFirstField e2e: cover the skip rules nothing was reaching\n\nFive gaps in the resolver''s coverage:\n\n* checkVisibility had NO test -- the \"skip\" case''s hidden field is a\n  HidingMode one, never rendered, so it only proved a missing element can''t\n  be chosen. Adds display:none and visibility:hidden fields that really are\n  in the DOM.\n* tabindex=\"-1\", an inert ancestor and an aria-hidden ancestor were all\n  untested. One case now puts each in front of the field that should win.\n* The radio preferChecked branch was untested; the model starts on the\n  third option, so \"first candidate\" and \"checked\" disagree.\n* A_second_form_in_the_same_scope_does_not_steal_focus_from_the_first was\n  true by construction -- one scope, one fire, nothing that could steal.\n  Renamed to what it actually shows, and joined by the case that makes it\n  non-trivial: form one''s only field disabled, so resolving \"first\" has to\n  cross the EditForm boundary into form two.\n\nAlso stabilizes the async case (its 250ms wait was shorter than\nPlaywright''s own NetworkIdle settle, so the test never saw the empty\nscope) and asserts the aria-disabled premise through the DOM, since\nPlaywright''s IsDisabledAsync folds aria-disabled into its own answer.","tree":{"sha":"7896566c1186ef9fc3aeb547334aa5e7d67c3666","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/7896566c1186ef9fc3aeb547334aa5e7d67c3666"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/9c030cb53e313d43512d1e8a932c59fb9d11b31f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/9c030cb53e313d43512d1e8a932c59fb9d11b31f","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKDljMDMwY2I1M2UzMTNkNDM1MTJkMWU4YTkzMmM1OWZiOWQxMWIzMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/ac08374b396d4c8455145da8cfe0982890bed062","sha":"ac08374b396d4c8455145da8cfe0982890bed062","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/ac08374b396d4c8455145da8cfe0982890bed062"}],"sha":"9c030cb53e313d43512d1e8a932c59fb9d11b31f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/9c030cb53e313d43512d1e8a932c59fb9d11b31f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/ac08374b396d4c8455145da8cfe0982890bed062/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:13:44Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:13:44Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"activateModal: offer the open to an in-panel FocusFirstField scope first\n\nWhich of activateModal and focusFirstField reached the DOM first was\ndecided by the module cache, so the first open and every reopen behaved\ndifferently. First open: wss-overlay.js is still importing when the scope\nfires, focus goes straight to the field. Reopen: the module is cached,\nactivateModal wins, and the measured sequence is\n`wss-modal-close >> ModalFirst` -- two moves, and a screen reader announces\nthe close button before the field the user came for.\n\nactivateModal now looks for a scope marker in the panel and calls\nWssEditControls.focusFirstField before its own initial-focus grab. The\nexisting \"is anything inside the panel focused?\" guard then decides what\nhappens, so there is no new failure mode: no WssEditControls, no field in\nthe scope, or a declined move all leave focus outside the panel and the\nnormal grab runs exactly as before.","tree":{"sha":"7d924e70d4fb75cdaebda898243f47892ec76ecc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/7d924e70d4fb75cdaebda898243f47892ec76ecc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/ac08374b396d4c8455145da8cfe0982890bed062","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/ac08374b396d4c8455145da8cfe0982890bed062","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKGFjMDgzNzRiMzk2ZDRjODQ1NTE0NWRhOGNmZTA5ODI4OTBiZWQwNjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/095cfb06ff2a7fb7f0db8da8d31ed8c052e53dea","sha":"095cfb06ff2a7fb7f0db8da8d31ed8c052e53dea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/095cfb06ff2a7fb7f0db8da8d31ed8c052e53dea"}],"sha":"ac08374b396d4c8455145da8cfe0982890bed062","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/ac08374b396d4c8455145da8cfe0982890bed062"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/095cfb06ff2a7fb7f0db8da8d31ed8c052e53dea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:12:17Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:12:17Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"FocusFirstField: a bounded retry, so asynchronous forms focus at all\n\nA scope that mounts before its fields do -- the ubiquitous \"load the model\nin OnInitializedAsync, render the form when it arrives\" page -- had an\nEMPTY scope on its single first-render attempt, so it focused nothing,\never. Same for fields behind display:none at first render.\n\nfocusFirstField now RETURNS whether the scope is settled: true when a field\nwas focused or one already held focus, false when there was nothing to aim\nat. FormDefaults re-attempts on later render batches while it keeps getting\nfalse, up to 10 attempts (MaxFocusAttempts), and stops permanently at the\nfirst attempt that finds a candidate.\n\nSettling on the first attempt with a candidate is what keeps the rest of\nthe contract: a form present from the start still fires exactly once on\nfirst render, and the \"never take focus off a field that already has it\"\nguard still applies to every attempt, so a late arrival cannot yank focus\nfrom a user who has started typing. The cap bounds both the cost of a scope\nthat never gets a field (10 querySelectorAll calls, not one per render\nforever) and how LATE an arrival may still move focus.","tree":{"sha":"f9a56177578dc29bc04a6d90f10628bee19c60e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/f9a56177578dc29bc04a6d90f10628bee19c60e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/095cfb06ff2a7fb7f0db8da8d31ed8c052e53dea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/095cfb06ff2a7fb7f0db8da8d31ed8c052e53dea","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKDA5NWNmYjA2ZmYyYTdmYjdmMGRiOGRhOGQzMWVkOGMwNTJlNTNkZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/f3770e5a3afc6a4c215da9070678d00de07f696f","sha":"f3770e5a3afc6a4c215da9070678d00de07f696f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/f3770e5a3afc6a4c215da9070678d00de07f696f"}],"sha":"095cfb06ff2a7fb7f0db8da8d31ed8c052e53dea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/095cfb06ff2a7fb7f0db8da8d31ed8c052e53dea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/f3770e5a3afc6a4c215da9070678d00de07f696f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:07:58Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:07:58Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"focusFirstField: aria-disabled is disabled, aria-readonly=\"false\" is not\n\nTwo candidates the DOM-side predicate got wrong, both measured in Chromium:\n\n* A disabled EditBool with AllowFocusWhenDisabled (the DEFAULT) renders\n  aria-disabled=\"true\" + tabindex=\"0\" and NO disabled attribute, so\n  el.disabled saw an ordinary focusable checkbox and focus landed on a\n  control the user cannot act on -- against the documented skip list.\n\n* Select renders readonly + an explicit aria-readonly=\"false\" while\n  ShowSearch=\"false\": readonly is only a typing guard there, and arrows,\n  Enter, Space and type-ahead all still change the value. Skipping it\n  stranded focus on the field AFTER a fully operable select.\n\nSo: aria-disabled=\"true\" now skips, and readonly skips only when the\nelement does not declare aria-readonly=\"false\". Three e2e cases\n(aria-disabled, select-no-search, multi-select-no-search) and the XML docs\nfollow.","tree":{"sha":"b6a8f36428b5e4bd84f227191f42af118419ddf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/b6a8f36428b5e4bd84f227191f42af118419ddf7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/f3770e5a3afc6a4c215da9070678d00de07f696f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/f3770e5a3afc6a4c215da9070678d00de07f696f","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKGYzNzcwZTVhM2FmYzZhNGMyMTVkYTkwNzA2NzhkMDBkZTA3ZjY5NmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/00c0affbe7d577727be607d5a7cadf6a18d0406d","sha":"00c0affbe7d577727be607d5a7cadf6a18d0406d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/00c0affbe7d577727be607d5a7cadf6a18d0406d"}],"sha":"f3770e5a3afc6a4c215da9070678d00de07f696f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/f3770e5a3afc6a4c215da9070678d00de07f696f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/00c0affbe7d577727be607d5a7cadf6a18d0406d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:05:57Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T04:05:57Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"FormDefaults: resolve IJSRuntime optionally, not through [Inject]\n\n[Inject] resolves during SetParametersAsync, long before anything checks\nwhether the default-off FocusFirstField feature is on -- and it throws when\nthe service is missing. That turned merely having <FormDefaults> in a tree\ninto a hard IJSRuntime dependency: true of every Blazor host, false of\nHtmlRenderer over a minimal service provider (email templates, PDF\npipelines, static HTML export), which now threw InvalidOperationException.\n\nInject IServiceProvider (always resolvable -- the container registers\nitself) and ask it for IJSRuntime at call time instead. Missing service =\nno focus move, the same degradation prerender already gets.\n\nFormDefaultsHtmlRendererTests renders the component through HtmlRenderer\nwith an EMPTY container, feature off and on; both cases threw before this.","tree":{"sha":"571c7827a9c9a7942077f460db1370054bf5a366","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/571c7827a9c9a7942077f460db1370054bf5a366"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/00c0affbe7d577727be607d5a7cadf6a18d0406d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/00c0affbe7d577727be607d5a7cadf6a18d0406d","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKDAwYzBhZmZiZTdkNTc3NzI3YmU2MDdkNWE3Y2FkZjZhMThkMDQwNmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/b811bdda0717d6c7a7a7e7a5321d44710f9ca9ec","sha":"b811bdda0717d6c7a7a7e7a5321d44710f9ca9ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/b811bdda0717d6c7a7a7e7a5321d44710f9ca9ec"}],"sha":"00c0affbe7d577727be607d5a7cadf6a18d0406d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/00c0affbe7d577727be607d5a7cadf6a18d0406d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/b811bdda0717d6c7a7a7e7a5321d44710f9ca9ec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T03:57:12Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T03:57:12Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"EditRadioEnum: the OtherValue box is a real field when it is bound\n\nThe second bound property had no ValueExpression, no FieldIdentifier, no\nFormOptions registration and never called NotifyFieldChanged -- so typing in the\n\"Other\" free-text box wrote the model and raised ZERO events. Anything driven off\nOnFieldChanged (FormAutoSave above all) silently lost the free text.\n\n@bind-OtherValue now supplies a new OtherValueExpression parameter. From it the\ncontrol derives a FieldIdentifier, registers the field under the box''s own\nelement id (other-{id}, kept in step with a runtime Id/IdPrefix change the same\nway SyncResolvedId does for the primary field), and notifies the EditContext on\nevery write to the property: the typed commit, the clear on a switch away from\nOther, and the re-commit on the way back. All three are writes to the bound\nproperty; leaving the last two silent would have reopened the same gap from the\nother side. Notification follows ValueChanged, never precedes it -- the validator\nreads the property live off the model during NotifyFieldChanged.\n\nAbsent the expression (a consumer wiring OtherValue/OtherValueChanged by hand)\neverything above stays off and the behavior is byte-identical to today. Opt-in by\nbinding rather than a throw.\n\nRelease-note-worthy: binding the pair also enrolls the property in the validation\nsummary. That is coherent -- an annotation on the OtherValue property previously\nproduced a message ValidationView had no registered field to link to; the link\nnow lands on the free-text input itself.\n\n10 bUnit facts, both paths.","tree":{"sha":"b0d33984ad236104a46da74e58d1a44ee3110fae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/b0d33984ad236104a46da74e58d1a44ee3110fae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/b811bdda0717d6c7a7a7e7a5321d44710f9ca9ec","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/b811bdda0717d6c7a7a7e7a5321d44710f9ca9ec","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKGI4MTFiZGRhMDcxN2Q2YzdhN2E3ZTdhNTMyMWQ0NDcxMGY5Y2E5ZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/4ba097c645b03ba1c04d72c8a0daf43b7f6469b3","sha":"4ba097c645b03ba1c04d72c8a0daf43b7f6469b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/4ba097c645b03ba1c04d72c8a0daf43b7f6469b3"}],"sha":"b811bdda0717d6c7a7a7e7a5321d44710f9ca9ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/b811bdda0717d6c7a7a7e7a5321d44710f9ca9ec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/4ba097c645b03ba1c04d72c8a0daf43b7f6469b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T03:50:56Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T03:50:56Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"FormAutoSave: one component replaces per-field @bind-Value:after\n\nA form-level auto-save that subscribes ONCE to EditContext.OnFieldChanged\ninstead of hanging a callback off every control. It sits inside the EditForm\n(after the validator) because the EditContext cascades down from EditForm --\nFormDefaults wraps an app/MFE root above it and cannot see one.\n\nPublic surface: OnSave (EventCallback<FormAutoSaveEventArgs>),\nDebounceMilliseconds (500, trailing; 0 fires per notification), SaveWhenInvalid\n(false), Concurrency (CoalesceTrailing | Concurrent), ShouldSave, OnSaveFailed,\nTimeProvider. Each closes a measured hazard: the debounce absorbs the keystroke\nstorm, the drag frames, the radio double-fire and the date-range pair; the\nvalidity gate swallows the parse-error false positive (and keeps its pending\nfields, so nothing is lost once the form is valid again); ChangedFields answers\n\"what changed\", de-duplicated in first-seen order.\n\nThe validity gate reads the context''s CURRENT messages rather than calling\nValidate(), which would light up every untouched field the moment one is typed\nin -- which is exactly why the component must sit after DataAnnotationsValidator.\n\nAn OnSave exception goes to OnSaveFailed when wired; otherwise it is re-raised\nthrough DispatchExceptionAsync, so an ErrorBoundary catches it and an unguarded\napp still fails loudly rather than losing it in the discarded debounce task.\n\nFieldChangedSubscription is the OnFieldChanged twin of ValidationStateSubscription\n-- same handler-identity discipline (SyncTo/Detach), rather than a fourth\nhand-rolled variant.\n\nTimeProvider is the testability seam: 18 bUnit facts drive the debounce off a\nhand-advanced clock, so not one of them sleeps.","tree":{"sha":"e682f108a6b5b02d170629726c68bb304ec1bba2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/e682f108a6b5b02d170629726c68bb304ec1bba2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/4ba097c645b03ba1c04d72c8a0daf43b7f6469b3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/4ba097c645b03ba1c04d72c8a0daf43b7f6469b3","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKDRiYTA5N2M2NDViMDNiYTFjMDRkNzJjOGEwZGFmNDNiN2Y2NDY5YjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/fed90a375b27db6c571a724f74822619fd2c8f23","sha":"fed90a375b27db6c571a724f74822619fd2c8f23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/fed90a375b27db6c571a724f74822619fd2c8f23"}],"sha":"4ba097c645b03ba1c04d72c8a0daf43b7f6469b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/4ba097c645b03ba1c04d72c8a0daf43b7f6469b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/fed90a375b27db6c571a724f74822619fd2c8f23/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T03:37:40Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T03:37:40Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"Pin the OnFieldChanged counts per gesture, per control family\n\nEight bUnit facts counting EditContext.OnFieldChanged invocations, so the\nmultiplicity a form-level auto-save has to absorb is measured rather than\nassumed. Measured: the three radio groups that forward ValueExpression to an\ninner InputRadioGroup (EditRadio, EditRadioEnum, EditRadioString) notify TWICE\nper click; EditBoolNullRadio notifies ONCE (it renders its own radios off\nEditControlBase, so there is no inner group). An EditNumber parse failure\nnotifies once while the model still holds the old value and the field is\ninvalid. The list family notifies exactly once per mutation -- checkbox toggle\nboth ways, an EditFile add batch, an EditFile remove, an EditMultiSelect pick.\n\nThe remove path is the one a hand-wired @bind-Value:after cannot reach at all:\nno bound field''s setter runs for it.","tree":{"sha":"641728fbd72aef47b107638ef14270d9a52c94b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/641728fbd72aef47b107638ef14270d9a52c94b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/fed90a375b27db6c571a724f74822619fd2c8f23","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/fed90a375b27db6c571a724f74822619fd2c8f23","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKGZlZDkwYTM3NWIyN2RiNmM1NzFhNzI0Zjc0ODIyNjE5ZmQyYzhmMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/d5cbb0e517b3ba04a0b00eacca3c84cbecf02a52","sha":"d5cbb0e517b3ba04a0b00eacca3c84cbecf02a52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/d5cbb0e517b3ba04a0b00eacca3c84cbecf02a52"}],"sha":"fed90a375b27db6c571a724f74822619fd2c8f23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/fed90a375b27db6c571a724f74822619fd2c8f23"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/d5cbb0e517b3ba04a0b00eacca3c84cbecf02a52/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T03:21:11Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T03:21:11Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"README: document FocusFirstField under FormDefaults\n\nIts own subsection: the precedence rule against FocusOnFirstRender, the skip\nlist, the once-per-instance firing (and why that is what makes the dialog\ncase work), the <template> markers'' one visible cost, and the accessibility\ntrade-off that makes it opt-in per scope rather than library-wide. Plus the\nthree cross-references that should reach it: the Quick Start script note, the\nModal/Drawer paragraph in Programmatic focus, and FocusOnFirstRender itself.\n\nNo changelog entry and no version bump -- the release-cut pass owns both.","tree":{"sha":"9ee9032d1eaf2e0ef81560411d3f193852e697c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/9ee9032d1eaf2e0ef81560411d3f193852e697c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/d5cbb0e517b3ba04a0b00eacca3c84cbecf02a52","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/d5cbb0e517b3ba04a0b00eacca3c84cbecf02a52","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKGQ1Y2JiMGU1MTdiM2JhMDRhMGIwMGVhY2NhM2M4NGNiZWNmMDJhNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/2399abaa2645ba296f0a65f963c135f507274397","sha":"2399abaa2645ba296f0a65f963c135f507274397","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/2399abaa2645ba296f0a65f963c135f507274397"}],"sha":"d5cbb0e517b3ba04a0b00eacca3c84cbecf02a52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/d5cbb0e517b3ba04a0b00eacca3c84cbecf02a52"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/2399abaa2645ba296f0a65f963c135f507274397/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T03:21:05Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T03:21:05Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"FocusFirstField coverage: 13 bUnit facts, 11 e2e, and the /focus-first-field page\n\nbUnit owns the C# half only -- the resolution chain, the once-per-instance\nfiring, the marker pair and its ids, and the byte-identical default-off\nmarkup. It cannot own the rest: bUnit''s JS interop is a recorder, so it can\nshow the call was issued but never that focus landed.\n\ne2e owns everything about document.activeElement, one scenario per ?case=\non the new test-only route (default case is the feature-OFF one, so \"changes\nnothing when unset\" runs against a plain visit): the plain form, the three\nskip rules in front of the target, an explicit FocusOnFirstRender on a later\ncontrol winning and STAYING won, a second form in the same scope, a second\narmed scope, an empty scope not reaching past its own closing marker, and the\nModal/Drawer opens -- each asserted both at the instant and 500ms later, plus\na focusin log whose tail must be the field.","tree":{"sha":"3c911ef9b5e5920fa99a255f8ea684967f82cd82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/3c911ef9b5e5920fa99a255f8ea684967f82cd82"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/2399abaa2645ba296f0a65f963c135f507274397","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/2399abaa2645ba296f0a65f963c135f507274397","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKDIzOTlhYmFhMjY0NWJhMjk2ZjBhNjVmOTYzYzEzNWY1MDcyNzQzOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/db27430898696ebd6bd13d543ad91c1fe6baaa91","sha":"db27430898696ebd6bd13d543ad91c1fe6baaa91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/db27430898696ebd6bd13d543ad91c1fe6baaa91"}],"sha":"2399abaa2645ba296f0a65f963c135f507274397","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/2399abaa2645ba296f0a65f963c135f507274397"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/db27430898696ebd6bd13d543ad91c1fe6baaa91/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T03:20:56Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T03:20:56Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"FormDefaults.FocusFirstField: focus a form''s first field, resolved in the DOM\n\nOpt-in (bool?, default off), following FormDefaults'' existing instance ->\ncascaded -> built-in resolution chain. The form-level counterpart to a\ncontrol''s FocusOnFirstRender: \"first\" then follows the markup instead of\nbeing pinned to whichever control happens to be written first.\n\nSeam: FormDefaults renders two empty <template> markers around its\nChildContent -- but ONLY while the feature resolves true, so the default-off\nrender tree stays byte-identical -- and fires once from OnAfterRenderAsync''s\nfirstRender, by which point the whole batch is in the DOM. JS\n(WssEditControls.focusFirstField) picks the first candidate between the\nmarkers in document order. Deliberately not a C#-side field registry:\nBlazor notifies non-fixed cascading-value subscribers in construction order,\nnot document order, so a C# answer would be wrong whenever markup order and\nconstruction order disagree -- and the skip rules (disabled, readonly,\ntabindex=-1, inert/aria-hidden ancestor, not rendered/visible) can only be\nanswered by the DOM anyway.\n\nThe JS declines to move focus when a field already holds it. That single\nguard settles three collisions: an explicit FocusOnFirstRender inside the\nscope wins in either order, a second armed scope can''t steal from the first,\nand the user can''t be yanked out of a field. Buttons deliberately do not\nblock it, so an overlay''s close X and a router''s focus-on-navigate heading\ndon''t suppress the feature -- measured sequence on a Modal open is\n`open-modal >> ModalFirst`, one move, with activateModal standing down.\n\nBest-effort throughout via JsInteropEc.InvokeBestEffortAsync: no JS,\nprerender, or an unreachable edit-controls.js all mean focus simply doesn''t\nmove.","tree":{"sha":"ebef44a42ebcd4f2886b3e52d416541a63f6fff3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/ebef44a42ebcd4f2886b3e52d416541a63f6fff3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/db27430898696ebd6bd13d543ad91c1fe6baaa91","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/db27430898696ebd6bd13d543ad91c1fe6baaa91","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKGRiMjc0MzA4OTg2OTZlYmQ2YmQxM2Q1NDNhZDkxYzFmZTZiYWFhOTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/61151117e00b1f11e1fa5a254b5ef979a9c0d3e3","sha":"61151117e00b1f11e1fa5a254b5ef979a9c0d3e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/61151117e00b1f11e1fa5a254b5ef979a9c0d3e3"}],"sha":"db27430898696ebd6bd13d543ad91c1fe6baaa91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/db27430898696ebd6bd13d543ad91c1fe6baaa91"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/61151117e00b1f11e1fa5a254b5ef979a9c0d3e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T02:19:29Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T02:19:29Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"AttributeSplat.RestExcept: case-insensitive removal, matching the presence check\n\nThe presence check (rest.ContainsKey) uses the same OrdinalIgnoreCase comparer as Blazor''s\nCaptureUnmatchedValues dictionary, but the removal loop compared with plain Ordinal -- so a\ncase-variant withheld key (onKeyDown, aria-Label) was detected as present and then never\nactually stripped. Invisible at the four event chain sites (Blazor''s own case-insensitive\nduplicate-attribute rule discards the leftover splatted frame, and ConsumerEvent''s lookup on\nthe original AdditionalAttributes is already case-insensitive), but Select''s aria-label\nre-homing genuinely leaked a duplicate onto the roleless wrapper. Tests added for both: a\ncase-variant event key (still invoked exactly once) and a case-variant aria-Label (no longer\nduplicated onto the wrapper).","tree":{"sha":"30a17b416b25a3d56442ffeb554cadbbaeaba307","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/30a17b416b25a3d56442ffeb554cadbbaeaba307"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/61151117e00b1f11e1fa5a254b5ef979a9c0d3e3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/61151117e00b1f11e1fa5a254b5ef979a9c0d3e3","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKDYxMTUxMTE3ZTAwYjFmMTFlMWZhNWEyNTRiNWVmOTc5YTljMGQzZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/6176fd5171f4058e8a0308438164d30fd355f32a","sha":"6176fd5171f4058e8a0308438164d30fd355f32a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/6176fd5171f4058e8a0308438164d30fd355f32a"}],"sha":"61151117e00b1f11e1fa5a254b5ef979a9c0d3e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/61151117e00b1f11e1fa5a254b5ef979a9c0d3e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/6176fd5171f4058e8a0308438164d30fd355f32a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T02:19:19Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T02:19:19Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"ConsumerEvent: dispatch EventCallback<EventArgs> and bare Func<Task>\n\nTwo legal splatted-attribute shapes fell through InvokeAsync''s switch to the no-op default:\na consumer handler typed to the base EventArgs (which the Razor compiler emits as\nEventCallback<EventArgs>, a different closed generic than the exact EventCallback<TArgs>\ncase matches) and a bare no-argument Func<Task>. Both now dispatch, with a test per shape.\n\nAction<object> and Func<object, Task> already invoked via delegate contravariance through\nthe existing Action<TArgs>/Func<TArgs, Task> cases -- adding explicit cases for those is\ndead code the compiler rejects outright (CS8120), so they stay undocumented as their own\ncase but are called out in the remarks. A mismatched EventCallback<TOther> (TOther other\nthan EventArgs) has no reachable path: EventCallback<T> isn''t variant, and its AsUntyped()\nescape hatch is internal to Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.","tree":{"sha":"e8e7173f2a8538322888d1d93f1bc7afd2433aca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/e8e7173f2a8538322888d1d93f1bc7afd2433aca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/6176fd5171f4058e8a0308438164d30fd355f32a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/6176fd5171f4058e8a0308438164d30fd355f32a","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKDYxNzZmZDUxNzFmNDA1OGU4YTAzMDg0MzgxNjRkMzBmZDM1NWYzMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/d7e6d4c66a0cb487286377d03bb0459d4f2bd3a6","sha":"d7e6d4c66a0cb487286377d03bb0459d4f2bd3a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/d7e6d4c66a0cb487286377d03bb0459d4f2bd3a6"}],"sha":"6176fd5171f4058e8a0308438164d30fd355f32a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/6176fd5171f4058e8a0308438164d30fd355f32a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/d7e6d4c66a0cb487286377d03bb0459d4f2bd3a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T02:19:06Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T02:19:06Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"overlay: activateModal initial-focus guard excludes the panel itself\n\nNode.contains(x) returns true for x === the node, and the panel is itself a legal focus\ntarget (it carries a tabindex for the focus trap). Without the `!== panel` check, a panel\nthat already holds focus when activateModal runs reads as \"already focused inside,\" and\ninitial focus is skipped entirely instead of moving to the first focusable child. A\ngenuinely pre-focused child still wins, unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"fff84c708df142d28772f5aed9a2080f2785f020","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/fff84c708df142d28772f5aed9a2080f2785f020"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/d7e6d4c66a0cb487286377d03bb0459d4f2bd3a6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/d7e6d4c66a0cb487286377d03bb0459d4f2bd3a6","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKGQ3ZTZkNGM2NmEwY2I0ODcyODYzNzdkMDNiYjA0NTlkNGYyYmQzYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/a0354df0a72bbee099460e3394d1e18ed5383f5a","sha":"a0354df0a72bbee099460e3394d1e18ed5383f5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/a0354df0a72bbee099460e3394d1e18ed5383f5a"}],"sha":"d7e6d4c66a0cb487286377d03bb0459d4f2bd3a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/d7e6d4c66a0cb487286377d03bb0459d4f2bd3a6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/a0354df0a72bbee099460e3394d1e18ed5383f5a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T01:49:30Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T01:49:30Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"README: the null-attribute-erasure fix is now library-wide, not EditString/EditNumber-only\n\nUpdates the \"Name collisions\" section to describe the contract across every single-editor\ncontrol (EditString, EditNumber, EditTextArea, EditDateNative, EditSelect, EditSelectEnum,\nEditSelectString, EditBool, EditRange), documents EditBool''s AllowFocusWhenDisabled-aware\nvariant and EditRange''s aria-disabled-in-place-of-disabled variant, and names the controls\nthat were swept and found structurally immune (EditFile, the checkbox/radio group\ncontrols, the Select engine, the date pickers) instead of leaving them as an open gap.","tree":{"sha":"390bb66c8692d0ce435715fd662a117995c50b99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/390bb66c8692d0ce435715fd662a117995c50b99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/a0354df0a72bbee099460e3394d1e18ed5383f5a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/a0354df0a72bbee099460e3394d1e18ed5383f5a","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKGEwMzU0ZGYwYTcyYmJlZTA5OTQ2MGUzMzk0ZDFlMThlZDUzODNmNWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/51c1085e809dde442d4c207c5db990e8ad2d4498","sha":"51c1085e809dde442d4c207c5db990e8ad2d4498","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/51c1085e809dde442d4c207c5db990e8ad2d4498"}],"sha":"a0354df0a72bbee099460e3394d1e18ed5383f5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/a0354df0a72bbee099460e3394d1e18ed5383f5a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/51c1085e809dde442d4c207c5db990e8ad2d4498/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T01:49:25Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T01:49:25Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"EditorAttributeOwnershipTests: 37 more facts, one per newly-adopted control\n\nExtends the EditString/EditNumber attribute-ownership pins (3d5ed90) to EditTextArea,\nEditDateNative, EditSelect, EditSelectEnum, EditSelectString, EditBool and EditRange --\neach gets the sharp case (an enabled/optional/valid field keeps the consumer''s splatted\ndisabled/aria-required/aria-errormessage) and the library-wins case, following the\nexisting file''s Render*/Splat helper pattern. EditBool additionally covers the\nAllowFocusWhenDisabled matrix (native disabled must stay absent under the default,\nreappear when the opt-in is off) and pushes its invalid-state test through a\nValidationMessageStore directly, since [Required] on a non-nullable bool never actually\nfails DataAnnotations validation. EditRange asserts aria-disabled where the others assert\ndisabled, since its field is a <div> with no native disabled attribute.\n\n2561 -> 2598 tests green, no new warnings.","tree":{"sha":"da0bd619f172d0ea35ee6ea79de54a4a1f599c23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/da0bd619f172d0ea35ee6ea79de54a4a1f599c23"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/51c1085e809dde442d4c207c5db990e8ad2d4498","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/51c1085e809dde442d4c207c5db990e8ad2d4498","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKDUxYzEwODVlODA5ZGRlNDQyZDRjMjA3YzVkYjk5MGU4YWQyZDQ0OTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/b1e776ce604342f744011f1f4adee924f2200dd3","sha":"b1e776ce604342f744011f1f4adee924f2200dd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/b1e776ce604342f744011f1f4adee924f2200dd3"}],"sha":"51c1085e809dde442d4c207c5db990e8ad2d4498","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/51c1085e809dde442d4c207c5db990e8ad2d4498"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/b1e776ce604342f744011f1f4adee924f2200dd3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T01:49:17Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T01:49:17Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"EditRange: fold aria-disabled/aria-* into the merged splat, track chaining intact\n\nSame erasure fixed elsewhere: the role=\"slider\" track wrote aria-disabled/aria-required/\naria-invalid/aria-errormessage explicitly beside its splat, so a null/false library value\ndeleted a consumer''s splatted same-named attribute rather than declining to override it.\nA <div> has no native `disabled`, so a new TrackStateAttributes uses aria-disabled in that\nslot (the rest matches EditControlBase.EditorStateAttributes exactly) and folds into\nTrackAttributes alongside the existing onclick/onkeydown consumer-event chaining, which\nis untouched.","tree":{"sha":"e746302d4a0ac22af42031955c4a65e9cf9a2fe3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/e746302d4a0ac22af42031955c4a65e9cf9a2fe3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/b1e776ce604342f744011f1f4adee924f2200dd3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/b1e776ce604342f744011f1f4adee924f2200dd3","node_id":"C_kwDOMEjYbtoAKGIxZTc3NmNlNjA0MzQyZjc0NDAxMWYxZjRhZGVlOTI0ZjIyMDBkZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/bf5eaa2342cbfa20220aa9a3622caacc17067ee5","sha":"bf5eaa2342cbfa20220aa9a3622caacc17067ee5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/bf5eaa2342cbfa20220aa9a3622caacc17067ee5"}],"sha":"b1e776ce604342f744011f1f4adee924f2200dd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/b1e776ce604342f744011f1f4adee924f2200dd3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/commits/bf5eaa2342cbfa20220aa9a3622caacc17067ee5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T01:49:12Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T01:49:12Z","email":"dcblakesley@gmail.com","name":"David Blakesley"},"message":"EditBool: fold disabled/aria-disabled/aria-* into the merged splat, AllowFocusWhenDisabled intact\n\nSame erasure fixed elsewhere, with a control-specific twist: EditBool''s disabled/aria-\ndisabled pair has its own shape because of AllowFocusWhenDisabled (default true), which\ndeliberately withholds the native `disabled` attribute so the checkbox stays a real Tab\nstop while non-operable. A new CheckboxStateAttributes writes disabled EXPLICITLY as\ntrue-or-false (never just omitted) whenever the checkbox is non-operable, so a consumer''s\nsplatted `disabled` can never quietly defeat that guarantee -- the merge happens in plain\nC# before any RenderTreeBuilder call, so this is an ordinary deterministic dictionary\noverwrite, not the duplicate-frame erasure the rest of this fix is about. While the\ncheckbox IS fully operable, neither key is written at all, so a consumer''s own disabled/\naria-disabled survive untouched -- the common case the erasure bug used to break.\nAllowFocusWhenDisabled''s existing contract (FocusApiTests) is unchanged and still green.","tree":{"sha":"c50fe9b05d9ffdb5283dfdf3c63721ab0d2e0a1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/trees/c50fe9b05d9ffdb5283dfdf3c63721ab0d2e0a1f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dcblakesley/Controls/git/commits/bf5eaa2342cbfa20220aa9a3622caacc17067ee5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17915296?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley","id":17915296,"login":"dcblakesley","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3OTE1Mjk2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dcblakesley","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls/commit/bf5eaa2342cbfa20220aa9a3622caacc17067ee5","node_id":"C_kwD